## What changed

**`rust/src/lib.rs`** — added `filter_by_tag` (after `ordered_pinned_first`):

```rust
/// Returns the notes whose `tags` contain exactly `tag` (exact match, not
/// substring), preserving their relative order.
pub fn filter_by_tag<'a>(notes: &'a [Note], tag: &str) -> Vec<&'a Note> {
    notes
        .iter()
        .filter(|n| n.tags.iter().any(|t| t == tag))
        .collect()
}
```

Exact match via `n.tags.iter().any(|t| t == tag)` — not a substring check. Order preserved by iterating `notes` in order.

**`rust/src/main.rs`** — the `list` command now parses an optional `--tag <TAG>` flag:
- Added `Note` to the `notekeep` import.
- The `list` branch scans `args[2..]`, pulling out `--tag <value>` (value at `i+1`), and passes the rest through unchanged. When `--tag` is present, output is run through `notekeep::filter_by_tag(&notes, tag)`; otherwise it lists all notes (original behavior).

